ation from the following statements.\n\nIf $X$ represents the number of customers arriving in a randomly selected $60$-minute period, then the test statistic is\n$X = 30$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} Since $P($ {{field-3}} $)$ {{field-4}} $1%$, there is {{field-5}} evidence to reject $H_{0}$.Therefore, we {{field-6}} that the customer arrival rate has reduced since the prices were increased."}] :knowledge-point/title "Conducting a Left-Tailed Test" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049302 :topic/math-academy-id 4126 :topic/title "Hypothesis Tests for the Rate of a Poisson Distribution"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192660 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191469} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191470} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191471} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191472}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191474} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191475} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191476} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191477}] :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191479} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #e