tion table below, where $X∼Po(6)$.\n\n| $x$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ | $14$ | $15$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $P(X \\le x)$ | $0.9574$ | $0.9799$ | $0.9912$ | $0.9964$ | $0.9986$ | $0.9995$ |\n\nBy assuming that every client is served independently, fill in the missing information from the following statements.\n\nIf $X$ represents the number of clients served on a randomly selected day, then the test statistic is\n$X = 13$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} Since $P($ {{field-3}} $)$ {{field-4}} $1%$, there is {{field-5}} evidence to reject $H_{0}$.Therefore, we {{field-6}} that the number of clients served per day has increased since the plumbing company performed an advertising campaign."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191521} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191522} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191523} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191524}] :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191520} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "insufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191526} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sufficient" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191527}] :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191529} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191530} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X \\ge 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191531} {:answ